BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-fm969-corridor-study-100225-20251002@calendars.changesaround
 me.com
DTSTAMP:20260904T145749Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251002T160000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251002T190000
SUMMARY:TxDOT: FM 969 Corridor Study (Elgin)
LOCATION:Spiderwood Studios 140 Utley Road Elgin\, TX 78621
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/austin/2025/fm969-corr
 idor-study-100225.html
DESCRIPTION:In-person meeting\; materials also posted online\nPublic commen
 t deadline: 3 Nov 2025.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: The purpose of this open house 
 is to share community feedback received during the first open house\, gath
 er input on preliminary improvement options\, and share next steps. In-per
 son open house attendees will be able to review hard copies of project mat
 erials\, ask questions of CAMPO\, TxDOT staff and consultants\, and leave 
 written comments. Online participants will be able to view the same inform
 ation delivered at the in-person public meeting. The virtual meeting will 
 consist of a self-guided virtual meeting room with pre-recorded narration 
 and will include both audio and visual components as well as opportunities
  to provide comments.\n\nDescription: The FM 969 Corridor Study will help 
 CAMPO and TxDOT more clearly define\, identify\, evaluate\, and recommend 
 potential design concepts for FM 969 from SH 130 in East Travis County to 
 SH 71 just west of Bastrop County.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.cam
 potexas.org/local-plans-and-studies/campo-project-readiness-program/fm-969
 -corridor-study/
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-102325-20251023@calendars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260904T145749Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251023T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251023T103000
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Public Transportation Advisory Committee
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/public-transportation/
 2025/102325.html
DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - online materials only\; materials post by 10a
 m (no in-person meeting)\n\n—\n\nPurpose: TxDOT invites the public to at
 tend a public meeting of TxDOT’s Public Transportation Advisory Committe
 e (PTAC).\n\nDescription: PTAC is a nine-member legislatively appointed co
 mmittee that advises the Texas Transportation Commission about public tran
 sportation-related matters. The committee’s meetings are open to the pub
 lic. The public can listen and view meeting presentations electronically v
 ia Teams.\nEach PTAC meeting includes an opportunity for anyone in attenda
 nce to address the committee. The Teams meeting\, however\, allows attende
 es to listen/view presentations only. Meeting documents\, including agenda
 s and printed transcripts of previous meetings\, are posted on TxDOT’s P
 TAC webpage.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.txdot.gov/about/advisory-
 committees/public-transportation-advisory-committee.html
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-102425-20251024@calendars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260904T145749Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251024T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251024T100000
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Bicycle and Pedestrian Advisory Committee Quarterly Meeting
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/public-transportation/
 2025/102425.html
DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - online materials only\; materials post by 9:3
 0am (no in-person meeting)\n\n—\n\nPurpose: TxDOT invites the public to 
 attend an in person and virtual public meeting of TxDOT’s Bicycle and Pe
 destrian Advisory Committee.\n\nDescription: TxDOT's Bicycle and Pedestria
 n Advisory Committee (BPAC) advises the Transportation Commission on bicyc
 le and pedestrian issues to help ensure the bicyclist’s and pedestrian
 ’s perspective will be considered in the development of departmental pol
 icies affecting bicycle use and pedestrian activity\, including the design
 \, construction\, and maintenance of roadways. The BPAC is comprised of bi
 cycle and pedestrian enthusiasts who represent various backgrounds and per
 spectives from across the state. Eleven members are selected by the Commis
 sion to serve voluntary\, three-year terms.\nThe Committee's meetings are 
 open to the public. Meeting documents\, including agendas and transcripts 
 of previous meetings\, are posted on TxDOT’s BPAC webpage.\n\n—\n\nPro
 ject info: https://www.txdot.gov/about/advisory-committees/bicycle-pedestr
 ian-advisory-committee.html
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-texas-statewide-multimodal-transit-plan-102025-20251113@cale
 ndars.changesaroundme.com
DTSTAMP:20260904T145749Z
DTSTART;TZID=America/Chicago:20251113T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Chicago:20251113T193000
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Texas Statewide Multimodal Transit Plan virtual public meeti
 ng with in-person options
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/public-transportation/
 2025/texas-statewide-multimodal-transit-plan-102025.html
DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - online materials\; materials post by 5pm (no 
 in-person meeting)\nPublic comment deadline: 20 Nov 2025.\n\n—\n\nPurpos
 e: As our state’s population and economy continue to grow\, TxDOT has be
 en developing the Statewide Multimodal Transit Plan ( Texas SMTP 2050 ) to
  help Texans get to where they want to go more effectively\, efficiently a
 nd safely while meeting the needs of our fast-growing state and contributi
 ng to a next-generation transportation network. With input from stakeholde
 rs and communities across the state\, this plan presents a coordinated\, u
 nified vision for multimodal transportation priorities through 2050 and be
 yond. The SMTP includes transit such as buses\, trains\, ferries\, and on-
 demand rideshare. TxDOT is hosting a series of public meetings and seeking
  public feedback on the development of the SMTP.\n\nDescription: Between O
 ct. 22 and Nov. 13\, TxDOT is hosting seven public meetings across the sta
 te to provide the public information about the Statewide Multimodal Transi
 t Plan ( Texas SMTP 2050)\, ask the technical team questions about the dra
 ft plan\, and provide feedback on the initial priority steps proposed for 
 implementation.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.txdot.gov/projects/pro
 jects-studies/statewide/statewide-multimodal-transit-plan.html\n\nMore: ht
 tps://www.txdot.gov/projects/projects-studies/statewide/statewide-multimod
 al-transit-plan.html
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
