BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:txdotev-hm-stip-fy-2025-2028-feb-revision-20260310@calendars.changesaro
 undme.com
DTSTAMP:20260904T145749Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260310
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Statewide Transportation Improvement Program for FY 2025 - 2
 028 - February revision
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/statewide/2026/stip-fy
 -2025-2028-feb-revision.html
DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - online materials only\; no fixed time (no in-
 person meeting)\nPublic comment deadline: 23 Mar 2026.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: 
 To receive public comments on the proposed February 2026 Revision to the S
 tatewide Transportation Improvement Program (STIP) for FY 2025 - 2028.\n\n
 Description: The STIP identifies federally funded transportation projects 
 included in the FY 2025–2028 Transportation Improvement Programs (TIPs) 
 for each Metropolitan Planning Organization (MPO) in Texas. It also includ
 es state and federally funded projects in nonattainment areas—Dallas-For
 t Worth\, El Paso\, Houston\, and San Antonio—as well as federally funde
 d projects in rural areas outside MPO boundaries and other statewide progr
 ams.\nFederal law (Title 23 USC §§134 and 135) requires MPOs and states 
 to develop TIPs and STIPs to secure federal transportation funding. These 
 plans must be developed in cooperation with MPOs\, transit operators\, and
  local officials and must include opportunities for public participation a
 nd approval by the governor or designee.\nA copy of the proposed February 
 2026 Revision to the FY 2025–2028 STIP will be available for review when
  this notice is published on TxDOT's website.\n\n—\n\nProject info: http
 s://www.txdot.gov/projects/planning/stip.html
CATEGORIES:hearing
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
