DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260414
SUMMARY:TxDOT: Notice of Availability for Finding of No Significant Impact 
 (FONSI) - RM 620 / Anderson Mill Road from South of Foundation Road to Lit
 tle Elm Trail
LOCATION:Travis and Williamson counties
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/austin/2026/noa-fonsi-
 rm620-anderson-mill-road.html
DESCRIPTION:Purpose: This notice advises the public that TxDOT has issued a
  Finding of No Significant Impact (FONSI) for the proposed RM 620/Anderson
  Mill Rd Intersection Improvement Project\, and that the FONSI is availabl
 e for public review. The proposed project would include intersection impro
 vements at RM 620 and Anderson Mill Road from approximately 240 feet south
  of Foundation Road to Little Elm Trail in Travis and Williamson counties\
 , Texas.\n\nDescription: The FONSI and approved final Environmental Assess
 ment (EA) are on file and available for inspection Monday through Friday b
 etween the hours of 8 a.m. and 5 p.m. at the Austin district office\, 7901
  N Interstate Hwy 35\, (512) 832-7000. They are also available online on t
 his webpage.\nFor further information or to request a copy of the FONSI an
 d or approved final EA\, please contact Rehan Bhatti\, Transportation Engi
 neer\, at 512-832-7221 or email .\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://ftp.txdo
 t.gov/pub/txdot/get-involved/aus/rm-620/041426-notice.pdf
CATEGORIES:engagement
X-CAM-ORG:txdotev
END:VEVENT
