SUMMARY:TxDOT: FM 969 Corridor Study from SH 130 to SH 71
LOCATION:on Wednesday\, April 15\, 2026: Spiderwood Studios 140 Utley Road 
 Elgin\, TX 78621
URL:https://www.txdot.gov/projects/hearings-meetings/austin/2026/fm969-corr
 idor-study-041526.html
DESCRIPTION:In-person meeting\; materials also posted online\nPublic commen
 t deadline: 18 May 2026.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: The purpose of this open house
  is to share community feedback received during the first two open houses\
 , gather input on proposed improvement concepts\, and share next steps. In
 -person open house attendees will be able to review hard copies of project
  materials\, ask questions from CAMPO\, TxDOT staff and consultants\, and 
 leave written comments. Online participants will be able to view the same 
 information delivered at the in-person public meeting. The virtual meeting
  will consist of a self-guided virtual meeting room with pre-recorded narr
 ation and will include both audio and visual components as well as opportu
 nities to provide comments.\n\nDescription: The Capital Area Metro Plannin
 g Organization (CAMPO) and TxDOT are working together to identify\, evalua
 te\, and recommend potential design concepts for FM 969 (Farm to Market 96
 9) from SH 130 in East Travis County to SH 71 in Bastrop County.\n\n—\n\
 nProject info: https://www.campotexas.org/local-plans-and-studies/campo-pr
 oject-readiness-program/fm-969-corridor-study/
