 s along 13 miles of I-35 from SH 29 to SH 45 North in Williamson County\, 
 Texas.\n\nDescription: The I-35 Georgetown to Round Rock Project proposes 
 to:\n- Add two non-tolled high-occupancy vehicle managed lanes in each dir
 ection\n- Add one mainlane in each direction between SH 29 and RM 1431\n- 
 Relocate and modify entrance and exit ramps\n- Reconstruct several bridges
  and cross street intersections\n- Add bypass lanes where needed\n- Add sh
 ared-use paths throughout the corridor\nAny environmental documentation\, 
 studies\, maps or drawings showing the project location and design\, tenta
 tive construction schedules and other information regarding the proposed p
 roject are on file and available for inspection Monday through Friday betw
 een the hours of 8 a.m. and 5 p.m. at 7901 N. I-35\, Austin\, TX 78753 or 
 by calling 512-939-3953. These materials will also be available in hard co
 py form for review at the in-person meeting and online on this webpage.\n\
 n—\n\nProject info: https://www.txdot.gov/mobility35/projects/i35-george
 town-to-round-rock.html
