DESCRIPTION:Virtual meeting - pre-recorded video presentation only\; materi
 als post by 5:30pm (no in-person meeting)\nPublic comment deadline: 16 Sep
  2026.\n\n—\n\nPurpose: TxDOT and the city of Round Rock are proposing i
 mprovements to US 79 from I-35 to east of A.W. Grimes Boulevard in William
 son County\, Texas. This notice advises the public that TxDOT will be host
 ing a virtual public meeting.\n\nDescription: The proposed improvements in
 clude widening the existing US 79 highway to add a third travel lane in ea
 ch direction with a raised median and selected median breaks\, constructin
 g intersection improvements featuring grade separations at Mays Street and
  at A.W. Grimes Boulevard\, reconfiguring the US 79 and I-35 intersection\
 , modifying driveways and access points to improve safety and traffic flow
 \, and installing shared-use paths on both sides of US 79 to enhance pedes
 trian and bicycle accommodations.\n\n—\n\nProject info: https://www.txdo
 t.gov/projects/projects-studies/austin/us79-i35-east-fm1460.html
